{"id":"p04-l06","minutes":35,"summary":"Bayes’ rule says how a measurement should change what you believe. You derive it from the definition of conditional probability, apply it to a door sensor with false positives, and implement a histogram filter that localises a robot in a corridor by alternating sensing and moving.","html":"<h2 id=\"deriving-bayes-rule\">Deriving Bayes’ rule</h2>\n<p>Conditional probability is defined by <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">∩</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">∣</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span>. Write the same joint probability both ways and divide:</p>\n<div class=\"math-scroll\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">∣</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.044em;\">z</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:2.363em;vertical-align:-0.936em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.427em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.314em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.044em;\">z</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.23em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"frac-line\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.677em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.044em;\">z</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">∣</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.936em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:2em;\"></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.044em;\">z</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:2.344em;vertical-align:-1.294em;\"></span><span class=\"mop op-limits\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.05em;\"><span style=\"top:-1.856em;margin-left:0em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.05em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">x</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6828em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.786em;margin-right:0.0714em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.5em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size3 size1 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">′</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.05em;\"></span><span><span class=\"mop op-symbol large-op\">∑</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.294em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.044em;\">z</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">∣</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.0519em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8019em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.113em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">′</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8019em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.113em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">′</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mord\">.</span></span></span></span></span></div>\n<p>Read it as: <strong>posterior</strong> ∝ <strong>likelihood</strong> × <strong>prior</strong>. <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span></span></span></span> is the state you care about (where the robot is) and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.044em;\">z</span></span></span></span> is the measurement (the sensor says “door”). <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.044em;\">z</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">∣</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span> is the sensor model: how likely that reading is in each state. The denominator just normalises the result to sum to one.</p>\n<p>The base rate matters. A sensor that’s right 80 % of the time can still be wrong most of the time it fires if the thing it detects is rare.</p>\n<h2 id=\"the-histogram-filter\">The histogram filter</h2>\n<p>Split the world into cells and keep a belief <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8444em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">b</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3117em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">i</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> for each. Two steps alternate:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Sense</strong>: multiply each cell’s belief by the likelihood of the measurement in that cell, then normalise. Belief sharpens.</li>\n<li><strong>Move</strong>: shift the belief by the commanded motion and blur it by the motion uncertainty. That’s a convolution of the belief with the motion model (lesson 8 of Phase 03). Belief spreads.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Sensing gains information and moving loses it. Repeating the cycle localises the robot even though no single reading is enough. This is a discrete Bayes filter; the Kalman filter is the same idea with Gaussians, and the particle filter (lesson 12) does it with samples.</p>\n\n<figure class=\"fig\"><div class=\"fig-body\"><div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"bayes\" data-args=\"{}\"></div></div><figcaption>A robot in a 20-cell circular corridor with doors at cells 2, 6 and 13. Press Sense and Move 1 cell repeatedly: the belief (lime) concentrates around the robot’s true cell.</figcaption></figure>\n<h2 id=\"worked-example\">Worked example</h2>\n<p>A corridor of 20 cells has doors in 3 of them. The door sensor reports “door” with probability 0.8 in front of a door and 0.1 in front of a wall.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Prior: uniform, so <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">door cell</span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">3/20</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.15</span></span></span></span>.</li>\n<li>The sensor says “door”. The evidence is <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.044em;\">z</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.8</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.15</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.1</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.85</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.205</span></span></span></span>.</li>\n<li>Posterior that the robot is in front of some door: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.8</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.15/0.205</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.585</span></span></span></span>. Despite the “80 % accurate” sensor, there’s a 41.5 % chance it’s facing a wall.</li>\n<li>Per cell: each door cell goes from 0.05 to <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.8</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.05/0.205</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.195</span></span></span></span>, and each wall cell from 0.05 to <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.1</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.05/0.205</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.0244</span></span></span></span>.</li>\n<li>Move one cell and sense again. Only positions consistent with both readings and the known door spacing keep high belief. With this noisy sensor and a robot that slips 20 % of the time, the filter’s best guess is the true cell about 30 % of the time and within one cell about 57 % of the time, against 5 % for a blind guess. Better sensors or less slip sharpen that quickly, and Exercise 3 asks you to try.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"code-it-from-scratch\">Code it from scratch</h2>\n\n<div class=\"code-card\" data-code=\"0\"><div class=\"code-head\"><span class=\"fname\" translate=\"no\">histogram_filter.py</span><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-copy=\"0\">Copy</button><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-download=\"0\">Download</button></div><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code class=\"language-python\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">import</span> numpy <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">as</span> np\n\nN = <span class=\"hljs-number\">20</span>\nDOORS = {<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">6</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">13</span>}\nP_HIT, P_FALSE = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.8</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.1</span>                       <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># P(z=door | door), P(z=door | wall)</span>\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">sense</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">bel, z</span>):\n    is_door = np.array([i <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> DOORS <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> i <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">range</span>(N)])\n    like = np.where(is_door, P_HIT <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> z <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">else</span> <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> - P_HIT, P_FALSE <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> z <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">else</span> <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> - P_FALSE)\n    post = bel * like\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> post / post.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">sum</span>()\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">move</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">bel, step=<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>, p=(<span class=\"hljs-params\"><span class=\"hljs-number\">0.1</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.8</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.1</span></span>)</span>):\n    <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;&quot;&quot;Shift by step with undershoot/exact/overshoot probabilities p (circular corridor).&quot;&quot;&quot;</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">sum</span>(pk * np.roll(bel, step + k - <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>) <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> k, pk <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">enumerate</span>(p))\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> __name__ == <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;__main__&quot;</span>:\n    bel = np.full(N, <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> / N)\n    post = sense(bel, <span class=\"hljs-literal\">True</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(post[<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>] - <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.8</span> * <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.05</span> / <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.205</span>) &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">1e-12</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(post[<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>] - <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.1</span> * <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.05</span> / <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.205</span>) &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">1e-12</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">sum</span>(post[i] <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> i <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> DOORS) - <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.585366</span>) &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">1e-6</span>\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(<span class=\"hljs-number\">5</span>)\n    hits = near = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> trial <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">range</span>(<span class=\"hljs-number\">200</span>):\n        pos, bel = <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">int</span>(rng.integers(N)), np.full(N, <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> / N)\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> _ <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">range</span>(<span class=\"hljs-number\">40</span>):\n            z = rng.random() &lt; (P_HIT <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> pos <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> DOORS <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">else</span> P_FALSE)\n            bel = sense(bel, z)\n            <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(bel.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">sum</span>() - <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>) &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">1e-12</span>\n            pos = (pos + <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> + rng.choice([-<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>], p=[<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.1</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.8</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.1</span>])) % N\n            bel = move(bel)\n        bel = sense(bel, rng.random() &lt; (P_HIT <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> pos <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> DOORS <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">else</span> P_FALSE))\n        a = <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">int</span>(np.argmax(bel))\n        hits += <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">int</span>(a == pos)\n        near += <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">int</span>(<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">min</span>((a - pos) % N, (pos - a) % N) &lt;= <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">f&quot;peak on the true cell in <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{hits}</span>/200 runs, within one cell in <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{near}</span>/200 (chance: 10/200)&quot;</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> hits &gt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">40</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> near &gt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">100</span>                    <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># far above the 5 % a guess would get</span></code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"exercises\">Exercises</h2>\n\n<div class=\"exercise\"><div class=\"ex-q\"><p>A crack detector flags 95 % of cracked welds and 3 % of good ones. 1 % of welds are cracked. If it flags a weld, what is the chance the weld is cracked?</p>\n</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class=\"ex-s\"><p><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.2484em;vertical-align:-0.4033em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8451em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.655em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">0.95</span><span class=\"mbin mtight\">×</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">0.01</span><span class=\"mbin mtight\">+</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">0.03</span><span class=\"mbin mtight\">×</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">0.99</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.23em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"frac-line\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.394em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">0.95</span><span class=\"mbin mtight\">×</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">0.01</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.4033em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.1901em;vertical-align:-0.345em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8451em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.655em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">0.0392</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.23em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"frac-line\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.394em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">0.0095</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.345em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.242</span></span></span></span>. Three out of four flagged welds are fine; a second independent test is needed before scrapping parts.</p>\n</div></details></div>\n\n<div class=\"exercise\"><div class=\"ex-q\"><p>Why does the histogram filter need the move step to blur the belief? What goes wrong without it?</p>\n</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class=\"ex-s\"><p>Without blur, the filter assumes perfect motion. A single slip would put the robot in a cell the belief has already ruled out (probability near zero), and multiplication can never bring it back, so the filter gets stuck on a wrong answer. The blur keeps every plausible cell alive.</p>\n</div></details></div>\n\n<div class=\"exercise\"><div class=\"ex-q\"><p>In the code, change the motion model to slip 10 % of the time (0.05, 0.9, 0.05) in both the simulation and <code>move</code>. How does the hit rate change?</p>\n</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class=\"ex-s\"><p>With seed 5 it rises from 60/200 to 87/200 on the exact cell and from 114/200 to 144/200 within one cell. Less motion blur means each sensing step’s information survives longer.</p>\n</div></details></div>\n<h2 id=\"quiz\">Quiz</h2>\n\n<div class=\"quiz\" data-quiz=\"p04-l06\"></div>\n\n","toc":[{"id":"deriving-bayes-rule","title":"Deriving Bayes’ rule"},{"id":"the-histogram-filter","title":"The histogram filter"},{"id":"worked-example","title":"Worked example"},{"id":"code-it-from-scratch","title":"Code it from scratch"},{"id":"exercises","title":"Exercises"},{"id":"quiz","title":"Quiz"}],"quiz":[{"id":"p04-l06-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>Door prior 0.15, P(door reading | door) = 0.8, P(door reading | wall) = 0.1. After one door reading, what is P(door)?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Posterior = likelihood × prior / evidence.</p>\n","answer":0.58537,"tol":0.001,"unit":""},{"id":"p04-l06-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>The crack detector example. What is P(cracked | flagged)?</p>\n","explain":"<p>The low base rate dominates.</p>\n","answer":0.24235,"tol":0.002,"unit":""},{"id":"p04-l06-q3","type":"mc","q":"<p>In a Bayes filter, the sensing step…</p>\n","explain":"<p>Measurement update = likelihood × prior.</p>\n","options":["spreads the belief","multiplies the belief by the likelihood and normalises","shifts the belief by the motion","resets the belief to uniform"],"answer":1},{"id":"p04-l06-q4","type":"mc","q":"<p>The motion step in a histogram filter is mathematically a…</p>\n","explain":"<p>Each cell’s belief spreads to its neighbours according to the motion probabilities.</p>\n","options":["multiplication","convolution with the motion model","Fourier transform","normalisation"],"answer":1},{"id":"p04-l06-q5","type":"num","q":"<p>Uniform prior over 20 cells, door reading. What is the posterior of one wall cell?</p>\n","explain":"<p><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.1</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.05/0.205</span></span></span></span>.</p>\n","answer":0.02439,"tol":0.002,"unit":""},{"id":"p04-l06-q6","type":"mc","q":"<p>The denominator <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.044em;\">z</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span> in Bayes’ rule…</p>\n","explain":"<p>It’s the sum of likelihood × prior over all states.</p>\n","options":["is the most important term","normalises the posterior to sum to one","is always 0.5","is the prior"],"answer":1}],"code":[{"file":"histogram_filter.py","lang":"python","src":"import numpy as np\n\nN = 20\nDOORS = {2, 6, 13}\nP_HIT, P_FALSE = 0.8, 0.1                       # P(z=door | door), P(z=door | wall)\n\ndef sense(bel, z):\n    is_door = np.array([i in DOORS for i in range(N)])\n    like = np.where(is_door, P_HIT if z else 1 - P_HIT, P_FALSE if z else 1 - P_FALSE)\n    post = bel * like\n    return post / post.sum()\n\ndef move(bel, step=1, p=(0.1, 0.8, 0.1)):\n    \"\"\"Shift by step with undershoot/exact/overshoot probabilities p (circular corridor).\"\"\"\n    return sum(pk * np.roll(bel, step + k - 1) for k, pk in enumerate(p))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    bel = np.full(N, 1 / N)\n    post = sense(bel, True)\n    assert abs(post[2] - 0.8 * 0.05 / 0.205) < 1e-12 and abs(post[0] - 0.1 * 0.05 / 0.205) < 1e-12\n    assert abs(sum(post[i] for i in DOORS) - 0.585366) < 1e-6\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(5)\n    hits = near = 0\n    for trial in range(200):\n        pos, bel = int(rng.integers(N)), np.full(N, 1 / N)\n        for _ in range(40):\n            z = rng.random() < (P_HIT if pos in DOORS else P_FALSE)\n            bel = sense(bel, z)\n            assert abs(bel.sum() - 1) < 1e-12\n            pos = (pos + 1 + rng.choice([-1, 0, 1], p=[0.1, 0.8, 0.1])) % N\n            bel = move(bel)\n        bel = sense(bel, rng.random() < (P_HIT if pos in DOORS else P_FALSE))\n        a = int(np.argmax(bel))\n        hits += int(a == pos)\n        near += int(min((a - pos) % N, (pos - a) % N) <= 1)\n    print(f\"peak on the true cell in {hits}/200 runs, within one cell in {near}/200 (chance: 10/200)\")\n    assert hits > 40 and near > 100                    # far above the 5 % a guess would get"}]}